Z||000000||fieroburton||09-06-2001||09:23 PM||||i just got back from wendys and turned off my head lights. they both go down but the left one keeps turning (the little black nob)<BR>its loud and anoying and will not quit so i unpluged the baterry so it has no power .<BR>how can i fix this by tomarro or as soon as possible ?<BR>thanx||||reg||11
Z||000001||Cliff Pennock||09-06-2001||09:29 PM||||I think the relays is shot. Until you get a new one, you can disconnect the relay (a small black box near the headlight). Of course you will not be able to open/close that headlight then.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Tigger||09-06-2001||09:34 PM||||Disconnect the plug on the single blue wire to stop the motor, disconnecting the relay does the same but the single wire is a quick disconnect.  First check would be to try the relay from the opposite headlight to check if it's a relay problem.  I'm thinking the motor needs to be rebuilt or replaced.  I know <A HREF="http://www.rodneydickman.com" TARGET=_blank>www.rodneydickman.com</A>  offers rebuild kits.<p>[This message has been edited by Tigger (edited 09-06-2001).]||||reg||1
