Z||000008||Rodney||09-07-2001||08:30 AM||||David Solt &lt;solt@rsn.hp.com&gt;<P>This guy selll rebuilds. He buys my parts to rebuild them and will take your old ones in trade. If they are 87-88 there is no reason not to do them yourself as they are very easy to rebuild. <P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000009||Formula88||09-07-2001||08:39 AM||||Yeah, what Rodney said.  On my 88, I'd never touched the headlight motor,and it took about 20 minutes to do.  Most of that time was figuring out how to get the motor out of the car.  I could do it in under 10, now.  Best $8 I ever spent (go ahead and do both - If one's gone, the other's not far behind)||||reg||10
